examples.question_text:
From the list **quadrilateral, kite, trapezium, parallelogram, rhombus, rectangle, square**, give every name guaranteed by the marks.
(a)
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.7,every node/.style={font=\normalsize,text=black}]
\usetikzlibrary{decorations.markings}
\tikzset{eqA/.style={postaction={decorate,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.5 with {\draw[black] (0pt,-4pt)--(0pt,4pt);}}}},eqB/.style={postaction={decorate,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.5 with {\draw[black] (-2pt,-4pt)--(-2pt,4pt);\draw[black] (2pt,-4pt)--(2pt,4pt);}}}}}
\draw[black,eqA] (0,0)--(5,0);
\draw[black,eqB] (5,0)--(5,3);
\draw[black,eqA] (5,3)--(0,3);
\draw[black,eqB] (0,3)--(0,0);
\draw[black] (0.3,0)--(0.3,0.3)--(0,0.3);
\draw[black] (5,0.3)--(4.7,0.3)--(4.7,0);
\draw[black] (4.7,3)--(4.7,2.7)--(5,2.7);
\draw[black] (0,2.7)--(0.3,2.7)--(0.3,3);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(b)
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.7,every node/.style={font=\normalsize,text=black}]
\usetikzlibrary{decorations.markings}
\tikzset{eq/.style={postaction={decorate,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.5 with {\draw[black] (0pt,-4pt)--(0pt,4pt);}}}}}
\draw[black,eq] (0,0)--(3.8,0);
\draw[black,eq] (3.8,0)--(3.8,3.8);
\draw[black,eq] (3.8,3.8)--(0,3.8);
\draw[black,eq] (0,3.8)--(0,0);
\draw[black] (0.3,0)--(0.3,0.3)--(0,0.3);
\draw[black] (3.8,0.3)--(3.5,0.3)--(3.5,0);
\draw[black] (3.5,3.8)--(3.5,3.5)--(3.8,3.5);
\draw[black] (0,3.5)--(0.3,3.5)--(0.3,3.8);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(c) For the shape in (a), Eva says “rectangle” and Ben says “parallelogram”. Whose name is guaranteed?

examples.solution_text:
One possible sketch is:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\usetikzlibrary{decorations.markings}
\tikzset{eqA/.style={postaction={decorate,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.5 with {\draw[black] (0pt,-3pt)--(0pt,3pt);}}}},eqB/.style={postaction={decorate,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.5 with {\draw[black] (-2pt,-3pt)--(-2pt,3pt);\draw[black] (2pt,-3pt)--(2pt,3pt);}}}}}
\coordinate (P) at (0,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (3,1.2);
\coordinate (R) at (5,0);
\coordinate (S) at (3,-1.2);
\draw[black,eqA] (P)--(Q);
\draw[black,eqB] (Q)--(R);
\draw[black,eqB] (R)--(S);
\draw[black,eqA] (S)--(P);
\path (P) node[left] {$P$};
\path (Q) node[above] {$Q$};
\path (R) node[right] {$R$};
\path (S) node[below] {$S$};
\draw[black] (Q) ++(201.801:0.4) arc[start angle=201.801,end angle=329.036,radius=0.4];
\draw[black] (S) ++(30.964:0.4) arc[start angle=30.964,end angle=158.199,radius=0.4];
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The matching marks show $PQ=PS$ and $QR=RS$, so the shape is a kite. The marked interior angles at $Q$ and $S$ are both greater than $90^\circ$ and less than $180^\circ$.
